* mv_package — MVPKG, the MultiValue package manager client (UniData port).
* Copyright (C) 2026 Gordon Heydon.  GPL-2.0-only (see LICENSE).
*
* Same behaviour as the portable BP/MVPKG: resolve a package from the
* registry, download its release tar and install it into an account —
* pulling in its dependencies first.  The portable client reaches HTTP and
* JSON as intrinsics (the MVX http/json extensions); UniData has neither, so
* this port declares them as the cataloged seam functions (udt/HTTPGET,
* HTTPGETFILE, JSONDECODE, MAPFIELD) and uses UniData idioms (GETENV, the
* statement forms of OSREAD/OSWRITE, @SENTENCE for args).
*
* The verb is built on the cmd command framework: it declares its subcommands
* and dispatches to one handler subroutine each (MVPKG.INSTALL, MVPKG.INFO, …),
* which read @SENTENCE themselves.  A cut-down copy of cmd is bundled in
* CMD.BP so MVPKG runs standalone; the full mv_cmd overrides it when installed.
*
* Installing shells out (curl, tar, the native rebuild), so it needs the
* privilege to do so.  A package that carries a udt-callc/ contribution
* rebuilds the shared CallC library (via MVPKGOS "CALLC") when installed.
   CALL CMD.INIT("MVPKG", "MultiValue package manager")
   CALL CMD.ADD("INSTALL", "install a package (name); --source [<dir>] git-clones an editable working copy", "MVPKG.INSTALL")
   CALL CMD.ADD("INFO", "show a package's registry metadata (name)", "MVPKG.INFO")
   CALL CMD.ADD("LIST", "show installed (managed) packages", "MVPKG.LIST")
   CALL CMD.ADD("UPDATE", "upgrade installed packages to latest ({name})", "MVPKG.UPDATE")
   CALL CMD.ADD("REMOVE", "uninstall a package (name)", "MVPKG.REMOVE")
   CALL CMD.ADD("REGISTER", "adopt an already-installed package (name {version})", "MVPKG.REGISTER")
   CALL CMD.ADD("SEARCH", "find packages by name/description (term)", "MVPKG.SEARCH")
   CALL CMD.ADD("SETUP", "set the registry URL (url)", "MVPKG.SETUP")
   CALL CMD.ADD("CONFIG", "show the current registry URL", "MVPKG.CONFIG")
   CALL CMD.ADD("REBUILD", "rebuild the host's native library", "MVPKG.REBUILD")
   CALL CMD.ADD("INIT", "provision this account for package management ({url})", "MVPKG.INIT")
   CALL CMD.RUN
